FREE TOKEN'S MOST GENERAL SYSTEMS IDEA IS NOT MoE-SPECIFIC: dynamic control is represented as data inside a statically captured execution graph. Its cache misses, victim choices, valid counts and CPU/GPU assignments vary each token, while the graph topology remains reusable.

Test this as a bounded PhysicalDerivation optimization pattern in Bonfyre:
- separate graph/contract SHAPE from dynamic realization DATA;
- compile/capture the stable physical skeleton once when operator ABI, shapes and authority contract are unchanged;
- feed dynamic valid counts, index lists, resource assignments, cache selections, and weather-derived parameters as data;
- invalidate/recompile only on true shape/contract/toolchain/validity changes;
- preserve exact Evidence/WHY links from dynamic inputs to the occurrence;
- never let a captured graph become semantic authority.

Candidate targets: repeated provider/model invocation paths, YaFF/HVM2 physical graphs, format finalizers, repeated evidence folds, and other hot paths where topology is stable but per-occurrence selections change.

Proof gate: choose one repeated Bonfyre hot path and show N executions with changing dynamic assignments reuse one compiled/captured body while exact receipts differ and semantic validity remains intact.
